Date: Wed, 13 Jan 1993 18:07:09 +0100 (MET)
From: ggoebel@sun1.ruf.uni-freiburg.de (Garrett Goebel)
Subject: I&A: Justification of Prefix

This post is mainly in response to what I feel are Tim's negative
responses to the formation of this prefixed topic.

I should start by saying that I am surprised by the response this 
prefix has generated, and I for one am excited to have another new
topic to look into.

In response to Tim:

1) I have already addressed this in private, and will only touch on 
it here... When I stated that I believe that the lurkers are more 
interested in doing extropian related activities than debating the
issues, I meant only that perhaps the lurkers are the types who 
would rather hear the ideas hashed about with out involving themselves
in the debate... while going about their extropian related activities.
I DID NOT mean to imply that frequent posters do nothing but talk.
That is something Tim infered.

2) Tim's major point, as I understand it, is that ideas and activities
are already being addressed on a mid to long-range scale, and that 
short-term and current applications are not worthy of discussion... or
that such short-term discussion is already being delivered in the 
form of "tips" 

In short, I disagree.

I appears to me that most of the mid to long-range discussions of ideas
and activities are focused more on the philisophical implications of such
ideas and technologies, than on fleshing things out or determining how we
are going to get from now (the short term) to these long-term goals.

I would think that I&A topic area would be a good place to flesh out
technilogical and economic realities of such things as uploading.  Better
yet, it would allow those that want to get out of the philosphical
debates on such issues to do so.  A focus on how we as individuals are
reaching out to future technologies and opportunities TODAY, not what will
we have to deal with when we get there.

Sure, some topics might not fit in very well... as Tim mentioned, uploading
is way far away.  But if it doesn't fit in I&A then don't post it there.
As Tim said, that's the joy of the free market... if  people wish to use
I&A they will if they don't they won't.

_______
Next, I agree that within limit, it would not be to smart or useful to 
debate very short term ideas and activities.  But when Tim states:

 "We cannot reasonable expect casually introduced ideas to somehow
energize a large fraction..."--Tim

I can not help but pointing out that Tim is overly negative.  Who among
all of us would want to read a casually introduced idea?  On the other hand,
Well though out ideas like Doug's Hip PC, have attracted a lot of input,
criticism, and advice.  Albeit Doug may not care... but Nick puts it best
when he says that I&A is a good area to test the viability of ideas.

 "This list is a great place to do foresighted pre-filtering that combines
voluminous idea generation with economic and technical critique." --Nick

Nobody is asking Doug to reveal sensitive or secret information that could
hurt his plans... We are giving useful criticism.

I do agree that it would be dim to say the least to go into great detail
into short-term business ideas.  And that it would be better to do such
discussion face to face with specialist. 

But I would point out that many "specialist" are already on this list, and
that no one in there right mind is going to give away sensitive info in the
I&A topic area.  However, people with general and related ideas could find
each other by posting non-sensitive ideas with the I&A prefix.  In this
manner, specialists could be found and advice and "tips" exchanged, or
private discussion groups could be formed by interested partys to continue
discussions on a more private level.

Example:  I and David Jevans both seem interested in new styles of 
management and organizational structure.  If more people are interested,
perhaps we could form a more private exchange of ideas in that area...
without overburdening the list with noise only a few of us are interested in.

Tim and Nick both mentioned the idea of an extropian company for starting
up our own companies... that has been mentioned again and again...  That
is a topic that could be discussed in the short medium and long range
in I&A.

The major benifits that I see from the I&A topic area are:

a) more focus on application of extropian ideas
b) a way to find people with business interests
c) a very VALUABLE nexus of information exchange.

On point C) I would like to put some emphasis.  Tim and many others seem
to think that the only way to form a extropian company is by investing
dollars and cents.  I would point out that the ideas and knowledge that
we share with each other is more valuable than any investment that Doug
(for example) could receive from us.

Perhaps company is not the correct word.  But the flow of ideas and 
knowledge right now justify the recognition of the inter-relation of
extropian activies.  If you want to tack a formal company and stock
investment plan to it go ahead... but it isn't necessary.

Again, at the risk of sounding too flowery... why don't we work
to help each other realize our goals (and receive help ourselves to
meet our own)?


-- 
