could just as easily be substituted for magick)

White Magick related to all the "mapped" areas of knowledge, and Black 
Magick refered to the "unmapped" regions.  A practical example would be
chemistry vs. alchemy.  Or "fact" vs. "theory"  In this manner, research
(Astrophysics for example) could be classified as Black Magick.

To try to make this post relevant... 

Perhaps we could organize the technology areas into WhiteTech (tech
based by hard facts... and by hard I mean assumed facts that most of
us aggree to...) and BlackTech (tech that is more theoretical, harder
to prove, and pushes the envelope through newer stranger angles)

