Amara Graps suggested that list members post biographies.  As I
am new to the list, I think it might it mighty be a good idea to
follow Amara's example.  He is my abbreviated bio:

                         SANDY SANDFORT

I was born in 1946 in Liberty, Missouri (that's right, just like
the USofA, I was "Conceived in Liberty . . .").  I have an adult
daughter and a four year-old granddaughter.

I got my B.A. in Speech from the University of Missouri--Kansas
City, and my J.D. from the UMKC, School of Law.

I have been admitted to the State Bars of Missouri and Arizona,
but I no longer practice law.  (I like to think of myself as a
practicing "anti-lawyer.")  Since 1978 I have been involved in
various aspects of international business.  (Not nearly as
glamourous nor as remunerative as I would have liked.)

I have been a freelance writer for over sixteen years.  I have
contributed to three books, helped edit and produce a magazine
("Freedom Today") and a newsletter ("Free Market Reporter").  I
have written business plans and promotional and advertising
pieces. My articles have covered a wide range of financial and
other subjects.  They have appeared in magazines as diverse as
"Reason," "Moneyworld," "Soldier of Fortune," "Hustler Erotic
Video Guide," "Paintcheck" and most recently, the "Malaysian
Tatler" and "Mondo 2000."

I lived for nearly a year in Costa Rica.  While there, I taught
English as a second language at the U.S. Cultural Center.  This
included several levels of advanced English as well as courses on
creative writing and American culture.  I also taught private
individual and institutional students.

I recently returned to the San Francisco area after living in
Singapore for eight months.  I was there on business, but I found
time to act in a television series for the Chinese Drama division
of the Singapore Broadcasting Corporation.  (I played a villain
who got his just deserts in the end).

I used to be involved in libertarian politics and organizations
but haven't done any of that for a number of years.  I found that
my business and personal life were far more of a threat to the
state than when I was "getting out the vote" or waving a protest
poster.  I read less science fiction then I would like to, but
there are only so many hours in a day.  For fun, I have appeared
as an extra in a number of films and TV shows.  Lately, I have
been extremely broke which has allowed me to pursue my hobby of
being an antisocial recluse.  People usually have strong feelings
about me, one way or the other (mostly positive, I think), and
that's the way I like it.  No fence-straddlers for me, thank you.

S A N D Y  S A N D F O R T


